From 5632f77552d0ec524c807c03c949d1060ce638a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 05:04:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix review findings: authedFetch adoption, ConfirmDialog,
 enrollment check, a11y labels

Addresses the code-review findings that are actually attributable to this
PR's own new/redesigned files (not the pre-existing payment/auth/build
issues elsewhere on this branch, which are out of scope here):

- ContentPage.tsx, ClassroomPage.tsx, BlogAdminPage.tsx: every bare
  fetch('/api/admin/...') swapped for authedFetch() so these routes
  actually authenticate for real SSO-logged-in admins instead of 401ing.
  BlogAdminPage.tsx already imported authedFetch but wasn't using it on
  three of its five calls - same bug, just partially applied.

- New src/components/ui/confirm-dialog.tsx: a real ConfirmDialog matching
  the design system, since it didn't exist anywhere in the codebase
  (checked main too). Wired into ContentPage.tsx's lesson/module delete
  and BlogAdminPage.tsx's post delete, replacing native confirm().

- admin/students/[id]/lessons/[id]/override: now checks the student has
  an enrollment in the lesson's course before writing LessonProgress,
  matching the student-facing complete route's existing check. Was
  previously missing entirely - a real bug in code from this PR.

- LearnClient.tsx, ClassroomPage.tsx, ContentPage.tsx: aria-label (and
  aria-pressed/aria-expanded where relevant) added to every genuinely
  icon-only control - data saver toggle, panel switcher, reply-send,
  pin/unpin, delete announcement/question/lesson/module/option, quiz
  editor close, module expand/collapse.

- Removed website-polishing-images.patch from the repo root - a stray
  download artifact that should never have been committed.

Not addressed here, out of scope for this PR: the pnpm@11 packageManager
field, the free-enrollment/webhook payment bypasses, the next.config.ts
redirect blocking /digitika/:courseId/learn, the isBypass RBAC bug, and
the missing prisma/migrations history - none of that is in files this PR
introduced or substantially rewrote, so I don't have enough context to
safely fix it blind. UsersPage/RolesPage/DiscountsPage still use native
confirm() too but weren't flagged as part of this PR's own diff.
